    {
      "id": 137251,
      "name": "lutherbellhendricksv",
      "username": "lutherbellhendricksv",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lutherbellhendricksv/{size}/2350_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-03-13T12:37:04.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Pydro\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/48/1844_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Pydro:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>…when someone is making a suboptimal move in the tournament? We hear Christopher's reaction, \"No, don't move away, use Hypsersonic Assault for a third time!\" However, we can't see or hear your reaction.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Disclaimer: I am not Paul.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>For myself, though, what makes watching people playing Tactics (and many other games) interesting is seeing what decisions they make differently than what I would do in their shoes. Different players have different play styles.</p>\n<p>Unless you're talking about things that are <em>strictly</em> suboptimal, like dying with +1 Defense tokens in hand, or passing your last action instead of Dodging. Then I try not to get too much spit on the screen. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/stuck_out_tongue.png?v=12\" title=\":stuck_out_tongue:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":stuck_out_tongue:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:13:35.035Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
